class: runtime
profiles: standard
summary: D502 hosted/heap once the started flag is set takes its classes' lock around every slot it hands out and takes back, and gives it back each time: a freed slot is still the next its class hands out, a fresh chunk is mapped under the lock, a large block is a mapping of its own that takes none, and a block grows and is resized, all on one thread, where a lock left taken would hold the next allocation for ever
program: main.ldn
root: ../../../../..
status: 42
